    "databaseId": 3520317690,
    "number": 1758,
    "title": "Windows, Pixi, VS2022 v17.14: Increase opencv version from 4.9.0 to 4.10.0",
    "url": "https://github.com/ros2/ros2/issues/1758",
    "body": "### Generated by Generative AI\n\n_No response_\n\n### Operating System:\n\n```Microsoft Windows [Version 10.0.22631.5909]```\n\n### ROS version or commit hash:\n\nrolling\n\n### RMW implementation (if applicable):\n\n_No response_\n\n### RMW Configuration (if applicable):\n\n_No response_\n\n### Client library (if applicable):\n\n_No response_\n\n### 'ros2 doctor --report' output\n\nn/a\n\n### Steps to reproduce issue\n\ntrying to build ros2 (rolling branch) from source\nvisual studio version:  MSVC_VERSION = 1944 (Visual Studio 2022, ver 17.14)\n\nWhen build ros2 rolling with Visual Studio 2022, ver 17.14, it has an issue and can't find opencv. \n\nThe issue is fixed in this commit https://github.com/opencv/opencv/commit/6fb3f6333150a777e835fc7c48e49750591bf7fe and released in opencv v4.10.0, where current pixi is using v4.9.0.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nVS2022 (v17.14) build successfully\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nVS2022(v17.14) has an issue and can't find opencv.\n\n### Additional information\n\nIs it possible to upgrade opencv to v4.10.0 (only for pixi build)?",
    "bodyHTML": "<h3 dir=\"auto\">Generated by Generative AI</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><em>No response</em></p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Operating System:</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><code class=\"notranslate\">Microsoft Windows [Version 10.0.22631.5909]</code></p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">ROS version or commit hash:</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">rolling</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">RMW implementation (if applicable):</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><em>No response</em></p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">RMW Configuration (if applicable):</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><em>No response</em></p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Client library (if applicable):</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><em>No response</em></p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">'ros2 doctor --report' output</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">n/a</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Steps to reproduce issue</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">trying to build ros2 (rolling branch) from source<br>\nvisual studio version:  MSVC_VERSION = 1944 (Visual Studio 2022, ver 17.14)</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">When build ros2 rolling with Visual Studio 2022, ver 17.14, it has an issue and can't find opencv.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The issue is fixed in this commit <a class=\"commit-link\" data-hovercard-type=\"commit\" data-hovercard-url=\"https://github.com/opencv/opencv/commit/6fb3f6333150a777e835fc7c48e49750591bf7fe/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/opencv/opencv/commit/6fb3f6333150a777e835fc7c48e49750591bf7fe\">opencv/opencv@<tt>6fb3f63</tt></a> and released in opencv v4.10.0, where current pixi is using v4.9.0.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Expected behavior</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">VS2022 (v17.14) build successfully</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Actual behavior</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">VS2022(v17.14) has an issue and can't find opencv.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional information</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Is it possible to upgrade opencv to v4.10.0 (only for pixi build)?</p>",
